 many thanks to Jean-marc Vincent for this solution:

Mister Shabou,
                                                                                                      
It seems that your local hardware database on ES40 is corrupted. The
best and simple way to solve is to use clu_delete_member then
clu_add_member. It will take just few minutes.
                                                                                                      
In other way, your TruCluster version is no more supported: V5.1A PK3.
You should be in V5.1A PK6 at least. The best is to be in V5.1B PK4.
                                                                                                      
V5.1A is in PVS since March 1st 2004 and up to Jun 30th 2007. This means
that you must run with latest patch kit: PK6.
                                                                                                      
V5.1B is the current version and will be supported until at least 2011.
This means that your must run latest or latest-1 patch kit: PK4 or PK3.
                                                                                                      
See at http://h20219.www2.hp.com/services/cache/11810-0-0-225-121.aspx
for PVS version support informations.
                                                                                                      
Hope this will help you.



after 20 minutes and a clu_delete_member + a clu_add_member the member work fin





